<fandom-ad id="top_boxad"></fandom-ad><h2 id="Appearance" class="open-section" section="1" aria-controls="Appearance-collapsible-section" aria-pressed="false" aria-expanded="true" role="button"><div class="section-header-label">Appearance</div><a href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fescapethebackrooms.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FLevel_37.2%3Faction%3Dedit%26section%3D1%26uselang%3Den&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" class="section-edit-link" aria-label="à¹à¸à¹‰à¹„à¸‚" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-auth-modal="signin"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-small"><use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-small"></use></svg></a><div class="vertical-separator"></div><button class="chevron-wrapper" aria-controls="Appearance-collapsible-section" aria-label="à¸¢à¸¸à¸š" aria-pressed="false" aria-expanded="true"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-small chevron"><use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#wds-icons-menu-control-small"></use></svg></button></h2><section id="Appearance-collapsible-section" class="mobile-hidden">
<p>Level 37.2 looks mostly like <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Level_37" title="Level 37">Level 37</a> but with new locations, darker areas, and much more danger.
</p>
</section><div class="incontent_boxad fandom-ad-wrapper"><fandom-ad id="incontent_boxad_1"></fandom-ad></div><h2 id="Objective" class="open-section" section="2" aria-controls="Objective-collapsible-section" aria-pressed="false" aria-expanded="true" role="button"><div class="section-header-label">Objective</div><a href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fescapethebackrooms.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FLevel_37.2%3Faction%3Dedit%26section%3D2%26uselang%3Den&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" class="section-edit-link" aria-label="à¹à¸à¹‰à¹„à¸‚" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-auth-modal="signin"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-small"><use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-small"></use></svg></a><div class="vertical-separator"></div><button class="chevron-wrapper" aria-controls="Objective-collapsible-section" aria-label="à¸¢à¸¸à¸š" aria-pressed="false" aria-expanded="true"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-small chevron"><use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#wds-icons-menu-control-small"></use></svg></button></h2><section id="Objective-collapsible-section" class="mobile-hidden">
</section><h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Part_1:_Entering_the_Expanded_Poolrooms">Part 1: Entering the Expanded Poolrooms</span></h3>
<p>Once you first spawn in, you will find yourself in a big room with windows, and a hole that you must enter to proceed onto the rest of the Level. When you enter the next area, there will be a pool that has the <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Hydrolitis_Plague" title="Hydrolitis Plague">Hydrolitis Plague</a>. Then you will find a <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Floatie_Boat" class="mw-redirect" title="Floatie Boat">Floatie Boat</a>. Get in the <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Floatie_Boat" class="mw-redirect" title="Floatie Boat">Boat</a> and start travelling. Shortly in, the path will have no more water, which means you will have to take a ladder to go up to the <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Valve" title="Valve">Valves</a>. There are 4 <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Valve" title="Valve">Valves</a>, and all you need to do is turn them all on. They are on the right side as well. Once you turn on all the <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Valve" title="Valve">Valves</a>, the path will fill with water, and you will be able to continue on. You will then go down a very fast water path. In the next area, the water will be too low to continue. There will be a nearby ladder, and when you get up, the entrance to the first Dark Poolrooms area will be accessible. There will be 3 ladders, and you will arrive in the first Dark Poolrooms area after going down any one of them.
</p>
<div class="incontent_boxad fandom-ad-wrapper"><fandom-ad id="incontent_boxad_2"></fandom-ad></div><h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Part_2:_Visiting_the_Dark_Poolrooms">Part 2: Visiting the Dark Poolrooms</span></h3>
<p>In the Dark Poolrooms, you must go around and turn 4 <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Valve" title="Valve">Valves</a> in order to fill up a tank with water in it. There are also rooms that contain grass, fake outside walls, and giant mushrooms. These rooms resemble Level -33.5 from the <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="text" href="https://backrooms.fandom.com/es/wiki/Wiki_Backrooms">Spanish Backrooms Wiki</a>. Each area has one of these rooms. Just make sure you keep an eye out for the <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Clump" title="Clump">Clumps</a> in the Level. If it spots you, just hide in the water and he will leave you alone. Once all of the <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Valve" title="Valve">Valves</a> are turned, you can go back to the Expanded Poolrooms.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Part_3:_Back_on_the_Surface">Part 3: Back on the Surface</span></h3>
<p>When you get back to the Expanded Poolrooms, the water will be filled, and you will be able to get back in the <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Floatie_Boat" class="mw-redirect" title="Floatie Boat">Floatie Boat</a> and continue on. However, shortly into travelling, you run into another obstacle, which is a giant pit. You must then once again go up the ladder on the left or right and turn all the valves (this time there's 4 on the left and the right) there's also a bridge that will let you easily get to the other side. However, if you run on it, it will break so be careful. Once all the <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Valve" title="Valve">Valves</a> are turned, the pit will be filled, and you can get back in the <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Floatie_Boat" class="mw-redirect" title="Floatie Boat">Floatie Boat</a> and continue travelling. However, soon enough, there will be another obstacle. The path cuts off, so you must get the boat to the other side by lowering the water level. There will be another ladder that you must go up and the entrance to the second Dark Poolrooms area will be there.
</p>
<div class="incontent_boxad fandom-ad-wrapper"><fandom-ad id="incontent_boxad_3"></fandom-ad></div><h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Part_4:_Back_to_the_Dark_Poolrooms">Part 4: Back to the Dark Poolrooms</span></h3>
<p>The Second Dark Poolrooms area is similar to the first one, but with a different map layout and with 3 Valves instead of 4. It's the easiest area. However, there is <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Hydrolitis_Plague" title="Hydrolitis Plague">Hydrolitis Plague</a> in some parts of the Level. Turn all 3 valves and leave.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Part_5:_Back_to_the_Expanded_Poolrooms">Part 5: Back to the Expanded Poolrooms</span></h3>
<p>After leaving the second Dark Poolrooms area, go through the triangular entrance to get to the next part of The Expanded Poolrooms. There will be a hole, and inside is the <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Floatie_Boat" class="mw-redirect" title="Floatie Boat">Floatie Boat</a>. After travelling for a bit, you will run into yet again another obstacle. The water won't be high enough to proceed. So, you will have to take the nearby ladder, and then you will have to take the stairs and then you will arrive at the above part of this area. In this above part, the entrance to the third Dark Poolrooms area will be there.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Part_6:_Down_to_the_Dark_Poolrooms_Again">Part 6: Down to the Dark Poolrooms Again</span></h3>
<p>You know how it works. Same as last time, but just a different map layout. Except this time there are 7 valves instead of 4. Turn all 7 and leave.
</p>
<div class="incontent_boxad fandom-ad-wrapper"><fandom-ad id="incontent_boxad_4"></fandom-ad></div><h3><span id="Part_7:_Escape.21"></span><span class="mw-headline" id="Part_7:_Escape!">Part 7: Escape!</span></h3>
<p>Once you return to the Expanded Poolrooms, the water will be high enough to continue. At this point, you will no longer need the boat, so just get on the stairs and on the other side is a pool with 3 entrances to a big room. This big room has a bunch of colored slides with a staircase leading up to them. It also has a beach ball, and life savers from the original <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Level_37" title="Level 37">Level 37</a>. Go up the staircase and at the top is a room with all 4 of the slides. Enter one of the slides (doesn't matter which one) and you will find yourself in <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Level_Fun%2B" title="Level Fun+">Level Fun+</a>.
</p>
<h2 id="Items" class="open-section" section="10" aria-controls="Items-collapsible-section" aria-pressed="false" aria-expanded="true" role="button"><div class="section-header-label">Items</div><a href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fescapethebackrooms.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FLevel_37.2%3Faction%3Dedit%26section%3D3%26uselang%3Den&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" class="section-edit-link" aria-label="à¹à¸à¹‰à¹„à¸‚" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-auth-modal="signin"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-small"><use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-small"></use></svg></a><div class="vertical-separator"></div><button class="chevron-wrapper" aria-controls="Items-collapsible-section" aria-label="à¸¢à¸¸à¸š" aria-pressed="false" aria-expanded="true"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-small chevron"><use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#wds-icons-menu-control-small"></use></svg></button></h2><section id="Items-collapsible-section" class="mobile-hidden">
</section><h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Expanded_Poolrooms">Expanded Poolrooms</span></h3>
<p>There are no items that can be found here.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Dark_Poolrooms">Dark Poolrooms</span></h3>
<p>Only one Item can be found in the Dark Poolrooms, and they are scattered around the <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Tank" title="Tank">Tanks</a>. This Item is:
</p>
<ul><li><a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Flashlight" title="Flashlight">Flashlight</a></li></ul>
