<div class="incontent_boxad fandom-ad-wrapper"><fandom-ad id="incontent_boxad_7"></fandom-ad></div><h2 id="Trivia" class="open-section" section="21" aria-controls="Trivia-collapsible-section" aria-pressed="false" aria-expanded="true" role="button"><div class="section-header-label">Trivia</div><a href="https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fescapethebackrooms.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FLevel_37.2%3Faction%3Dedit%26section%3D7%26uselang%3Den&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section" class="section-edit-link" aria-label="à¹à¸à¹‰à¹„à¸‚" data-tracking-label="log-in-edit-section" data-auth-modal="signin"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-small"><use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#wds-icons-pencil-small"></use></svg></a><div class="vertical-separator"></div><button class="chevron-wrapper" aria-controls="Trivia-collapsible-section" aria-label="à¸¢à¸¸à¸š" aria-pressed="false" aria-expanded="true"><svg class="wds-icon wds-icon-small chevron"><use xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="#wds-icons-menu-control-small"></use></svg></button></h2><section id="Trivia-collapsible-section" class="mobile-hidden">
<ul><li>This Level only ever had one teaser, but it was for a Level -33.5 Area in the Dark Poolrooms.</li>
<li>The name for the Expanded Poolrooms was confirmed by <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Fancy" title="Fancy">Fancy</a> on Discord. He also brought up the name Poolrooms Expanded.</li>
<li>Despite Fancy's 10th <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Devlogs" title="Devlogs">Devlog</a> stating that this Level is called Level 37.2, searching for Level 37.2 leads to 0 results for the Sublevel. This is either an error on Fancy's end or the Level 37.2 page on Fandom got changed to <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="text" href="https://backrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Level_37.2?so=search">what it is now</a> and <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Fancy" title="Fancy">Fancy</a> actually meant to say it was <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="text" href="https://backrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Level_37.1">Level 37.1</a> or The Deep End. This is more accurate to the page he showed in the <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Devlogs" title="Devlogs">Devlog</a>.</li>
<li>It was believed that the large mushroom rooms teased by <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Fancy" title="Fancy">Fancy</a> meant <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Fancy" title="Fancy">Fancy</a> would add Level -33.5, also known as flotadores which is floaters in Spanish from the <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="text" href="https://backrooms.fandom.com/es/wiki/Wiki_Backrooms">Spanish Backrooms Wiki</a>. Later, when <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Fancy" title="Fancy">Fancy</a> released his 10th <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Devlogs" title="Devlogs">Devlog</a> after <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Part_4" title="Part 4">Part 4</a> released this may or may not meant to have been a reference to it.</li>
<li>This Level does not have an <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/Achievements" title="Achievements">Achievement</a> for completing it or a <a href="https://escapethebackrooms.fandom.com/wiki/The_Hub" title="The Hub">Hub</a> Entry.</li>
<li>There is a bug where the player can jump on the iron bar and land into the slides room, this way you can skip the Level.</li></ul>
